Z||000008||lowCG||10-28-1999||10:06 PM||||And subframe,A/C,tranny,tranny mounts,axles,alternator,but it's worth a try,sometimes one side will work,and that's half the battle in making your own.<BR>Never bothered to do anything to the 2.8,I'm planning something else so I don't have to rebuild, measure every little part and then hope that it holds up.I can find a complete 3.4 twincam for about the same $ as a rebuild,doesn't make sense to me to struggle with something else when an option like that is right there.<BR>Now if there were some really good brakes that would bolt on,I wouldn't be messing around with the M6,BMW calipers,and 11.5" rotors.<BR>Whenever I need to try something out,I go buy it,and if it doesn't work out,I return it. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
