Z||000017||fierosound||03-13-2000||02:03 PM||||Fieroshop - everybody "talks the talk" - good luck! (in a good way)<P>Fiero Parts and Appraisals is finding that out right now.  After an "enthusiastic" response on their announcement they were getting Borla systems produced, everyone silently disappeared when it came time to place FIRM ORDERS.  Check the message forums below.  I haven't seen too many names from this forum there...               <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>Of course, if you could produce a system for $150 ($300 with headers) I'm sure many people here would want a set, once you have them in-store, and can deliver within 2 days.  Right now, the genuine Borla system, which is recognized as making the best power producing exhaust systems, and that Fiero Parts and Appraisals is offering at $420, is the least expensive stainless steel exhaust system out there...             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I sent in my cash for CDN$770 - ouch!  But still cheaper than driving into a muffler shop and saying "Build me a new T304 stainless steel system, from manifold to tips".  The  guys here should get THAT estimate.  $420 won't look so bad after that!<P> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/002625.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/002625.html</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/002112.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/002112.html</A> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 03-14-2000).]||||reg||4
Z||000018||Tom88gt||03-14-2000||12:39 PM||||The S-10 headers won't work.  Trust me.  I had an S-10 that I put headers on.  There is no way you will make them fit.  Not even close.  Totaly different for a front engine/rear drive layout.  The headers are so long they will stick out the wheel wells and you won't have any rear tires.||||reg||13
Z||000019||Formula||03-14-2000||01:12 PM||||We should look for cavalier Z24 87-90 2.8 headers.  There is a large aftermarket resource for them.  <P>Would 3.1 headers work on a fiero?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000020||fierosound||03-14-2000||03:48 PM||||Formula<P>You won't find headers for any FWD car from GM - Corsica, Cavalier, etc.  They don't seem to exist - at least I haven't found any - and I've checked around alot.  They're harder to find than Fiero headers!  Like Borlas, if you want headers - you gotta pay for 'em!||||reg||10
